{:category :orientation, :timings {:predicted_ms 11020.112, :cache_n 72794, :predicted_per_second 83.12075231177324, :predicted_n 916, :prompt_per_token_ms 0.9713468208092486, :prompt_ms 504.129, :prompt_n 519, :prompt_per_second 1029.4984021946764, :predicted_per_token_ms 12.030689956331877}, :finish-reason "stop", :reasoning "We need to answer: \"What are the pre-registered KILL conditions and CONFIRM conditions for H1?\" The user asks: \"What are the pre-registered KILLS and CONFIRM for the active bet (H1)\". We must answer based on provided docs. The relevant doc is docs/current-mental-model/BETES.md? Actually the doc is docs/current-mental_model/BETS.md. Let's locate the relevant section.\n\nFrom the provided files:\n\n- docs/current-mental-model/BETs.md (the heading says \"BETS.md\" but the content is in docs/current-mental-model/BETE? Actually the file is named \"BETS.md\". It contains \"BETS — North & Bets\". It defines \"Authority rules\" and \"North — Sid's commitment\". Then \"The ladder — route hypotheses toward North\". Then \"H1 — ACTIVE · The trail ...\", includes \"Claim: a trail view ... Pre-registered evidence: KILL: two weeks after the view ... CONFIRM: the photograph-and-paste ritual ...\". So we need to extract the pre-registered evidence for H1: kill condition and confirm condition.\n\nThus answer: The pre-registered kill condition for H1 is that two weeks after the view first renders, new thinking panels still start on paper and wall photos still get pasted into LLM chats; the grace period is that form-break fix cycles are design, not failure, but the clock measures where new thinking starts, not polish. The confirm condition is that at least half of new panels or threads start inside Softland, i.e., the photograph-and-paste ritual replaced by context bundles from the view.\n\nThus answer: The kill condition: if after two weeks from first render new thinking still starts on paper or wall photos are still pasted, i.e., the form hasn't changed. The confirm condition: at least half of new thinking starts inside Softland via context bundles.\n\nThus answer accordingly. Also mention that these are pre-registered evidence conditions for killing or confirming H1.\n\nThus final answer: The pre‑registered kill condition for H1: after the first render, if within two weeks the system still shows new thinking starting on paper or users still paste wall photos into chats (i.e., the “photograph‑and‑paste ritual” persists), then H1 is considered killed. The pre‑registered confirm condition: if after that period at least half of the newly created panels/threads are generated from context bundles inside Softland (i.e., the ritual is replaced), then H1 is confirmed. Provide that answer.\n", :spine-gated? false, :usage {:completion_tokens 916, :prompt_tokens 73313, :total_tokens 74229}, :ts-ms 1783325318748, :wall-ms 11597, :qid "O3", :prompt-chars 275003, :ablation :A0, :subject "nemotron-30b-a3b-q8-128k-16kdry", :completion "**Pre‑registered kill condition (H1 – “The trail view beats the wall”)**  \n- **When?** Two weeks after the trail‑view first renders.  \n- **What must *not* happen?** New thinking must still start on paper **or** wall‑photos must still be pasted into LLM chats. In other words, the “photograph‑and‑paint‑the‑wall” ritual must still be in use.  \n- **Why it kills the bet:** If either of those conditions persists after the two‑week window, the hypothesis that “a trail view replaces the wall” is falsified, so the active bet is considered dead.\n\n**Pre‑registered confirm condition (H1)**  \n- **When?** After the same two‑week window has elapsed.  \n- **What must happen?** At least **half** of the newly created thinking panels/threads must originate from *context bundles* inside Softland (i.e., users are no longer reaching for the wall or external images; they are pulling the needed context directly from the trail view).  \n- **Why it confirms the bet:** When this threshold is met, the evidence supports the claim that the trail view is now the primary source of new thought, satisfying the pre‑registered success criterion.\n\nIn short:\n\n- **Kill condition:** > 2 weeks after first render → new thinking still originates on paper or via pasted wall images.  \n- **Confirm condition:** > 2 weeks after first_render → ≥ 50 % of new panels/threads are produced from Softland‑internal context bundles.  \n\nThese are the exact pre‑registered criteria recorded in **`docs/current-mental-model/BETs.md`** for the currently active bet (H1).", :model "nvidia_Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B-Q8_0.gguf"}
