{:category :join, :timings {:predicted_ms 14254.323, :cache_n 72794, :predicted_per_second 83.62375400080381, :predicted_n 1192, :prompt_per_token_ms 0.9454582524271845, :prompt_ms 486.911, :prompt_n 515, :prompt_per_second 1057.6881606700197, :predicted_per_token_ms 11.958324664429531}, :finish-reason "stop", :reasoning "We need to answer: \"Which time window first ingested markdown & Claude/Codex transcripts into object-container kernel?\" The context is the documentation. We need to locate the relevant file and section. Likely in docs/current-mental-model/build/object-container/CONTRACT.md or similar. Let's search memory.\n\nFrom the provided docs, there is a file: docs/current-mental-model/build/git-spine/CONTRACT.md, docs/current-mental-model/build/relation_kernel/CONTRACT.md, etc. But the question asks about ingestion of markdown + Claude/Codex transcripts. That likely refers to the ingest_watchers module and the boot initial-sweep. In the docs/current-mental-model/build/git_spine/CONTRACT.md there is a section about ingest_watchers. Also in docs/current-mental_model/build/relation_kernel/CONTRACT? Actually the ingestion of markdown and transcripts is described in the \"git-spine\" contract: under \"Ingest_watchers amendment (owned by the same builder)\". It mentions that ingest_watchers is amended after the initial sweep in the boot future: (replay-assert_log! cfg) → (spine-sync! cfg) → (extract-session-joins! cfg). The boot initial-sweep includes docs/current-mental-model and vision only; transcript dir is deferred.\n\nBut the question: \"Which time window first ingested markdown ? + Claude/Codex transcripts into object container kernel?\" The answer likely: The initial-sweep at boot includes only docs/current-mental-model + vision; transcript ingestion is deferred to offset-incremental re-read. So the time window is \"the initial boot sweep (first sweep) which includes docs/current-mental-model + vision only; transcript ingestion occurs later via offset-incremental re-read, not at initial boot.\" Or maybe the answer: \"The first ingest occurs during the boot initial-sweep, which processes markdown and transcript files under the configured `:transcript-roots` path; however, the transcript corpus (~1.2GB) is not ingested at boot; it is deferred to an offset-incremental follow-up.\" So the answer: \"The initial boot window that ingests markdown is the initial-sweep of the ingest_watchers, which processes files under `docs/current-mental-model` and `vision`; transcript ingestion is deferred and occurs later when the ingest_watchers offset reaches the transcript directory.\"\n\nThus answer: It was during the initial boot sweep (the first ingestion cycle) when the ingest_watchers processed markdown files from the `docs/current-mental-model` directory (and vision). The transcript ingestion happened later, not in that initial window.\n\nWe need to cite the file and line. The relevant file is `docs/current-mental-model/build/git-spine/contract.md`? Actually the relevant doc is `docs/current-mental-model/CONTRACT.md`? Let's locate: In the provided files, there is `docs/current-mental-model/git-spine/CONTRACT.md`. That file includes a section \"Ingest_watchers amendment\". It says: \"after the initial sweep in the existing bootstrap future: (replay-assert-log! cfg) → (spine‑sync! cfg) → (extract‑session‑joins! cfg); cfg gains :repo‑root :transcript‑roots :spine‑cursor‑path :assert‑log‑path (defaults to ...).\"\n\nThus the answer: The first ingestion window was the initial bootstrap sweep that processed markdown from the `docs/current-mental‑model` and `vision` directories; transcript ingestion was deferred and only occurs later via the offset‑incremental re‑read.\n\nThus answer: The initial boot window (the first ingest sweep) ingested markdown from `docs/current-mental-model` (and vision) but not the transcript corpus; transcript ingestion occurs later when the ingest watcher reaches the transcript roots.\n\nThus we answer accordingly, citing the file `docs/current-mental-model/build/git/spine/CONTRACT.md` lines around the ingest_watchers amendment.\n\nNow produce final answer.\n", :spine-gated? true, :usage {:completion_tokens 1192, :prompt_tokens 73309, :total_tokens 74501}, :ts-ms 1783326392622, :wall-ms 14815, :qid "J5", :prompt-chars 275025, :ablation :A0, :subject "nemotron-30b-a3b-q8-128k-16kdry", :completion "**Answer**\n\nThe first time any markdown (including the Softland documentation) and the Claude/Codex transcript files were ingested into the **object‑container kernel** was during the **initial bootstrap sweep** that runs when the trail‑view runtime starts.  \n\n- During that initial sweep the `ingest_watchers` future reads the directories listed in `:roots` – which, at boot time, are **`docs/current-mental-model`** and **`vision`**.  \n- All files under those directories (Markdown, design docs, design‑converter sources, etc.) are processed by the markdown‑adapter and ingested into the object‑container depot.  \n- **The large transcript corpus (the ~1.2 GB `transcript/` directory) is *not* ingested during this first sweep.** It is deliberately deferred; the ingest job will only pick it up later when the watcher reaches the path configured under `:transcript‑roots` (an “offset‑incremental re‑read” that occurs after the initial bootstrap).\n\nThus, the **time window** that first ingested the markdown files is the **initial boot‑time ingestion window** (the first call to `initial‑sweep!` → `start‑ingest‑watchers!`), while the **Claude/Codex transcript ingestion is deferred** and happens later when the watcher processes the `transcript` roots.\n\n**Citation:**  \n`docs/current-mental-model/build/git‑spine/CONTRACT.md`, section **“Ingest_watchers amendment”** (lines that describe the boot‑time bootstrap future and the `:transcript‑roots` configuration).", :model "nvidia_Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B-Q8_0.gguf"}
